      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Question",
        "Answer"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "How do we know Earth's interior structure?",
          "Seismology (P/S waves, shadow zones, normal modes), moment of inertia, geodesy, meteorites"
        ],
        [
          "What creates Earth's magnetic field?",
          "Convection + compositional buoyancy in liquid outer core → αΩ MHD dynamo"
        ],
        [
          "Why is Io so volcanic?",
          "Forced eccentricity (Laplace resonance 1:2:4) → tidal dissipation ~6×10¹³ W"
        ],
        [
          "Why does Europa have a liquid ocean?",
          "Tidal heating from Laplace resonance; evidence: induced magnetic field, young surface"
        ],
        [
          "Why does Mars lack a dynamo?",
          "Core cooled and solidified ~4 Gya; no inner core solidification to drive convection"
        ],
        [
          "Why does Venus lack plate tectonics?",
          "Insufficient water in mantle (lubrication), slow rotation (weak Coriolis for dynamo)"
        ],
        [
          "Why does Mercury have such a large core?",
          "Giant impact stripped silicate mantle; confirmed by MESSENGER geochemistry"
        ],
        [
          "What is the Fulton gap?",
          "Bimodal gap at ~1.7 R_E; photoevaporation removes H/He from borderline planets"
        ],
        [
          "How do we model exoplanet interiors?",
          "M-R diagram + EOS integration; degenerate without spectra"
        ],
        [
          "What seismic phase goes through Earth's center?",
          "PKIKP (P → outer core K → inner core I → back through K → P)"
        ],
        [
          "What is the CMB?",
          "Core-Mantle Boundary at 2891 km; V_S drops to zero (liquid below)"
        ],
        [
          "Adams-Williamson equation gives what?",
          "Density profile from seismic velocities assuming adiabatic compression"
        ]
      ]
    }
